# Operator preferences

This file stores operator-level preferences that AI agents read at the start of a session. It is not a governance document; it is personal settings for how the operator wants to interact with agents.

## Current preferences

- **aiLanguage** — language the AI uses for **all** communication with the operator in this session: questions, responses, summaries, reports, status updates, and any other chat output.
- **documentationLanguage** — default language for newly generated RFCs, ADRs, READMEs, and other project documentation.
- **register** — communication register (`business` | `creative`). Business = core behavioral layer only, professional and efficient. Creative = core + extended behavioral layer (RFC-0549) with creative partnership and emotional support.
- **formOfAddress** — form of address (`formal` | `informal`). Formal = "vy"/"Sie" in languages with a formal/informal distinction. Informal = "ty"/"du". Defaults to formal.

## Changing preferences

Run the `my-preferences` skill or edit this file directly. When an agent asks you to choose a language, your answer is saved here for future sessions.
